  "@type": "Capability",
  "critical": true,
  "description": "Multi-stage fractional distillation column for separating liquid mixtures by boiling-point differences. Vapor rising from the reboiler contacts liquid descending from the condenser on trays or packing; at each contact the more volatile component transfers to vapor and the less volatile to liquid. Three internal configurations serve different duties: bubble-cap trays (high turndown), sieve trays (lowest cost, most common), and packed columns (lowest pressure drop, preferred for vacuum and heat-sensitive service). The most important separation apparatus in chemical manufacturing, responsible for 40-60% of capital cost in a typical plant; enables petroleum refining, solvent purification, and silicon chlorosilane separation.",
  "early_win": false,
  "id": "chemistry.distillation-column",
  "level": "capability",
  "name": "Distillation Column",
